# Prototype 1 -- the first plant that is a *problem* rather than a diagram.
#
#   Deposit -> Mine -> OreBay ==[ Rail ]==> OreYard -> Smelter -> PlateBay
#                                                   -> GearPress -> GearBay -> Delivery
#
# Everything in configs/ before this one was built to stress the solver. This
# one is built to be annoying, and it is deliberately underbuilt in two places
# at once so that fixing the obvious problem exposes the next one.
#
# Rates as it stands:
#
#   Mine       1 x 50 / 60      = 0.833 ore  /tick
#   Rail       1 x 1000 / 2000  = 0.500 ore  /tick   <- first bottleneck
#   Smelter    2 x 25 / 50      = 1.000 plate/tick of appetite
#   GearPress  1 x 20 / 80      = 0.250 plate/tick of appetite  <- second
#   Delivery   1 x 50 / 100     = 0.500 gear /tick of appetite
#
# So it fails in a very specific order, and each failure looks different:
#
#   t ~ 0        everything runs; the plant looks fine
#   t ~ 12,000   OreBay fills, and the Mine goes BLOCKED
#   t ~ 16,000   PlateBay fills, and the Smelters go BLOCKED behind the press
#   thereafter   the whole plant runs at the press's 0.125 gear/tick
#
# A player who buys rail vehicles first has fixed the bottleneck that is no
# longer the bottleneck. That is the entire lesson of the scenario and it is
# not stated anywhere in it.
#
# # The deposit is a bay
#
# `Deposit` is a storage with contents and no producer wired to it, which is
# all a finite ore body is. It needed no new construct: when it empties, the
# Mine starves for the ordinary reason, and every part of the machinery that
# explains starvation explains this too. 50,000 crude ore is roughly 25,000
# gears if none of it is wasted, so the deposit is a real ceiling rather than
# scenery -- a player who over-builds mining burns through the field early.

item CrudeOre
item IronOre
item IronPlate
item Gear

blueprint GearWorks {
    storage Deposit     { capacity 50000  initial 50000 CrudeOre  policy round_robin }
    process Mine        { consumes 50 CrudeOre takes 60 ticks produces 50 IronOre }
    storage OreBay      { capacity 4000   policy round_robin }

    link    Rail        {
        moves 1000 IronOre
        distance 1600 speed 2 base 200      # 200 + 800 = 1000 ticks each way
    }

    storage OreYard     { capacity 4000   policy round_robin }
    process Smelter x2  { consumes 25 IronOre takes 50 ticks produces 25 IronPlate }
    storage PlateBay    { capacity 2000   policy round_robin }
    process GearPress   { consumes 20 IronPlate takes 80 ticks produces 10 Gear }
    storage GearBay     { capacity 2000   policy round_robin }
    sink    Delivery    { consumes 50 Gear every 100 ticks }

    wire Deposit -> Mine -> OreBay -> Rail -> OreYard -> Smelter -> PlateBay
    wire PlateBay -> GearPress -> GearBay -> Delivery
}

deploy 1 x GearWorks
